# English in the project

Code, comments, documentation, and commit messages are English.

## Write in English

- Identifiers, comments, `docs/`, `plans/`, `README.md`, and `AGENTS.md`.
- New error text that developers read in logs or thrown `Error` messages.

```ts
// Bad
// abre o link exportado e apaga

// Good
// Open the stored export URL and delete that item only.
```

## Leave user-facing copy in the catalogs

- Portuguese, Spanish, and English sentences for the local page live in `web/src/i18n/pt.ts`, `es.ts`, and `en.ts`.
- Do not translate those catalogs into English, and do not add a Portuguese comment next to them.
- Words from a Facebook export, such as `fev` or `compartilhou`, stay in the parser as data. Explain them with an English comment when the code is not obvious.
